Design for Testing in a remanufacturing context involves designing products so that their components can be efficiently inspected and tested for condition, performance, and remaining useful life without the need for full disassembly. This includes designing component geometries that are accessible to non-destructive testing (NDT) methods such as ultrasonic inspection, X-ray, eddy current testing, and visual inspection. Test points, diagnostic ports, and sensor interfaces should be integrated into the product architecture.